"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/5181","html_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/5181","diff_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/5181.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/5181.patch","merged_at":"2026-11-11T00:40:46Z"},"body":"Fixes #4071\n\n## Summary\n\n```text\nvalidate\n  reject inconsistent bounds, windows, fees, ledgers, rates, caps, and allowlists\nfold_authorisation\n  ignore invalid higher versions and retain the highest valid body\n```\n\n- Treat zero rate numerator, zero total cap, and an empty allowlist as invalid, consistent with the positive-rate and non-empty policy documentation.\n- Keep gateway checks (#3801), duplicate-version tie-breaking (#4069), and the separate signing-path concern (#4414) out of scope.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- **Before:** current main checked issuer identity and nonzero denominator only; issue #4071 documents malformed bodies that passed validation and folded as live.\n- **After:** added per-shape validation tests and a regression test proving an invalid higher version does not shadow a prior valid body. The targeted local cargo test is rerunning after its first build exceeded the 10-minute shell limit; results will be recorded on the task.\n\n## Merge Danger\n\n**Door:** two-way\n\n**Blast Radius:** small — rejects malformed or non-actionable authorisations at the existing validation gate.\n\n<!-- codesmith:footer -->\n---\n<a href=\"https://backend.blacksmith.sh/track/enable-autofix?expires=1796335808&installation_model_id=443529&pr_number=5181&ref=codesmith_pr_footer&repository=developing-today%2Fcode&return_to=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fdeveloping-today%2Fcode%2Fpull%2F5181&signature=463db334ae9097b0cb2d77a7df39e790ea61d410a4f924c951f60fd42b4f4958\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Autofix with [code]smith\" src=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark-3x.png\" width=\"190\" height=\"28\"></picture></a>\n<sup><a href=\"https://app.blacksmith.sh/developing-today/codesmith/code/pr/5181?autoLogin=true&ref=codesmith_pr_footer\">Open in [code]smith</a> · Need help on this PR? Tag <code>@codesmith-bot</code> with what you need.</sup>\n\n<!-- codesmith:autofix:disabled -->\n<!-- /codesmith:footer -->","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/5181/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/5181/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/14611","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/14611/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/14611/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/14611/events","html_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/14611","id":6591476667,"node_id":"PR_kwDOJWP4788AAAABRqgVVQ","number":14611,"title":"fleet session bind --force: replace a dead worktree binding in place","user":{"login":"dezren39","id":11225574,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMjI1NTc0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11225574?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39","html_url":"https://github.com/dezren39","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":1,"created_at":"2026-11-24T21:10:07Z","updated_at":"2026-11-25T03:28:13Z","closed_at":"2026-11-25T03:28:10Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/14611","html_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/14611","diff_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/14611.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/14611.patch","merged_at":"2026-11-25T03:28:10Z"},"body":"Part of #14454.\n\nA `.fleet-session-id` marker naming an ended session blocks every Fleet domain invocation from that worktree (`main.rs` dispatcher fails closed before the domain runs), and bare `fleet session bind` cannot self-heal — resolution fails before anything is persisted.\n\nThis slice adds `--force` to `fleet session bind`: it removes the worktree marker without validating it, then resolves normally (rebinds a supplied/env identity, else unattributed). Explicit flag rather than auto-clear on bare bind, because a liveness check answers false for unverifiable sessions too (unreachable server; connect builds without the probe) — only the operator asserts the binding is dead.\n\nEvidence\n- New oracle tests: `force_clears_before_resolving_and_rebinds_the_supplied_identity`, `stale_marker_still_fails_closed_without_force_and_clear_is_not_run`, `force_clear_failure_blocks_session_initialization`, `clear_marker_at_removes_the_marker_and_ignores_a_missing_one`, plus strict parser cases. `cargo test -p fleet --bin fleet`: 142 passed, 0 failed.\n- Live binary check in a scratch worktree with a stale marker: `fleet queue list` died with the exact issue error (`stale .fleet-session-id refers to ended or unverifiable session ...`); after `fleet session bind --force` (exit 0, marker gone) the same call reached the broker and listed tasks. `--force --session-id <live>` rewrote the marker in place.\n- Docs: `USAGE`, `pkgs/fleet/book/reference/builtins.md`, `pkgs/fleet/README.md` #9075 section. TS hosted transcription untouched (resolver semantics unchanged; `--force` is CLI-layer, no hosted bind CLI exists).\n\nWorker does not merge. The hatch-side marker still needs `fleet session bind --force` (or `rm .fleet-session-id`) run on that machine after this lands.\n\n<!-- codesmith:footer -->\n---\n<sup><a href=\"https://app.blacksmith.sh/developing-today/codesmith/code/pr/14611?autoLogin=true&ref=codesmith_pr_footer\">Open in [code]smith</a> · Need help on this PR? Tag <code>@codesmith-bot</code> with what you need.</sup>\n\n<!-- codesmith:autofix:disabled -->\n<!-- /codesmith:footer -->","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/14611/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/14611/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/3133","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/3133/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/3133/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/3133/events","html_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/3133","id":6136969263,"node_id":"PR_kwDOJWP4788AAAABL_CSTw","number":3133,"title":"fix(cold-store-reaper): fail closed on malformed S3 list pages (#2733)","user":{"login":"dezren39","id":11225574,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMjI1NTc0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11225574?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39","html_url":"https://github.com/dezren39","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":2,"created_at":"2026-10-31T16:10:36Z","updated_at":"2026-11-01T16:47:25Z","closed_at":"2026-10-31T18:38:28Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/3133","html_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/3133","diff_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/3133.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/3133.patch","merged_at":"2026-10-31T18:38:28Z"},"body":"Fixes #2733 (queue task 4414).\n\n`_parse_s3_list_page` in `pkgs/cold-store-reaper/cold_store.py` now fails closed:\n- Malformed XML → `ColdStoreError` (was raw `ET.ParseError` escaping past `main()`'s `ColdStoreError`-only handler).\n- Well-formed XML whose root is not `ListBucketResult` → `ColdStoreError` (was silently read as an empty bucket by backup/eviction code).\n- `Size` non-numeric (`abc`, `1.5`) or negative (`-5`) → `ColdStoreError` naming the entry key; missing/empty `Size` keeps the default 0.\n\nTests: new `TestS3ListPageValidation` (6 tests: non-XML body, wrong root, abc, 1.5, -5, missing-Size default, valid page with pagination token + aware LastModified). Full suite on laptop: `python3 -m unittest discover -s pkgs/cold-store-reaper/tests/` — 101 tests, OK (skipped=1).\n\n<!-- codesmith:footer -->\n---\n<a href=\"https://app.blacksmith.sh/developing-today/codesmith/code/pr/3133?autoLogin=true&ref=codesmith_pr_footer\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/view-with-codesmith-dark-v3.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/view-with-codesmith-light-v3.svg\"><img alt=\"View with [code]smith\" src=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/view-with-codesmith-dark-v3-3x.png\" width=\"162\" height=\"28\"></picture></a> <a href=\"https://backend.blacksmith.sh/track/enable-autofix?expires=1796055039&installation_model_id=443529&pr_number=3133&ref=codesmith_pr_footer&repository=developing-today%2Fcode&return_to=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fdeveloping-today%2Fcode%2Fpull%2F3133&signature=e358d565b7dc75166b43d8f67a7c66b8cc5e9c6af4b78c54373f3e0f3b52710b\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Autofix with [code]smith\" src=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark-3x.png\" width=\"190\" height=\"28\"></picture></a>\n<sup>Need help on this PR? Tag <code>@codesmith-bot</code> with what you need.</sup>\n\n<!-- codesmith:autofix:disabled -->\n<!-- /codesmith:footer -->","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/3133/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/3133/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/12651","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/12651/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/12651/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/12651/events","html_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/12651","id":6546140732,"node_id":"PR_kwDOJWP4788AAAABRF7dZg","number":12651,"title":"fix(fleet): shepherd packet prs entries are PR references (#12280)","user":{"login":"dezren39","id":11225574,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMjI1NTc0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11225574?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39","html_url":"https://github.com/dezren39","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":13198400136,"node_id":"LA_kwDOJWP4788AAAADEq-aiA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/labels/audit:complete","name":"audit:complete","color":"0e8a16","default":false,"description":"PR fully implemented spawning issue","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":2,"created_at":"2026-11-22T18:34:26Z","updated_at":"2026-11-24T01:57:30Z","closed_at":"2026-11-22T18:37:50Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/12651","html_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/12651","diff_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/12651.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/12651.patch","merged_at":"2026-11-22T18:37:50Z"},"body":"Follow-up to #12649 (Refs #12280).\n\nThe shepherd packet built by the coverage reconciliation carried `payload.prs` as bare numbers (`[950]`). The queue validator requires every `prs` element to be an object with a positive-integer `number` (#5549), so the fallback's enqueue would have failed validation at runtime. Caught by validating the first live backlog packets before enqueueing them — no invalid packet was ever enqueued.\n\n`prs` now carries `{number, url, title}` PR references, and the fixture test pins the exact shape. Verification: fleet-run of `test_check_coverage.py` on this branch (result in the #12280 completion comment).\n\n<!-- codesmith:footer -->\n---\n<a href=\"https://dashboardbackend.blacksmith.sh/track/run-proof?expires=1797964469&installation_model_id=443529&pr_number=12651&ref=codesmith_pr_footer&repository=developing-today%2Fcode&return_to=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.c