ain() does not catch, so the janitor died with a traceback and no refused run record -- the #6812 invisible-death mode, second door.\n\n- All three readers now validate shapes (page/row/item list+object checks, integer id/number via a shared _shape_int helper that rejects bools/dicts/non-numeric strings, payload must be an object, status must be a string) and raise SafetyError naming the reader and the bad field/shape. SafetyError is caught by main(), producing the refused run record and exit 2.\n- Well-formed inputs return identical results (control tests added).\n- Tests: RawQueueModule stub plus malformed-shape cases for all three readers (error-dict page, string row/item/claim/payload, missing/dict/non-int id/number, dict status, list scan, dict items), asserting SafetyError and that the message names the reader.\n\nVerified on the laptop: python3 infra/cargo-target-janitor/tests/test_cargo_target_janitor.py -- 35 tests, OK.\n\nQueue: task 11061 (repo-health-code-pilot), lane code-v.\n\n<!-- codesmith:footer -->\n---\n<a href=\"https://backend.blacksmith.sh/track/enable-autofix?expires=1796691016&installation_model_id=443529&pr_number=7005&ref=codesmith_pr_footer&repository=developing-today%2Fcode&return_to=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fdeveloping-today%2Fcode%2Fpull%2F7005&signature=1b4be49b72a3ecd369f8e6467e5931a6689744ff1de536da92425a645ebbc696\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Autofix with [code]smith\" src=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark-3x.png\" width=\"190\" height=\"28\"></picture></a>\n<sup><a href=\"https://app.blacksmith.sh/developing-today/codesmith/code/pr/7005?autoLogin=true&ref=codesmith_pr_footer\">Open in [code]smith</a> · Need help 